# Azure Deployment Plan — Sinhala Teaching AI Avatar

## 1. Current Project Assessment

### Component Inventory

| Component | Technology | Details |
|-----------|-----------|---------|
| **Frontend** | Next.js 16 + React 19 + TailwindCSS 4 | SSR app, 10 pages, calls backend API at `localhost:8000` |
| **Backend** | FastAPI + Uvicorn (Python 3.10) | 20+ REST endpoints, LangGraph supervisor pipeline |
| **Database** | MongoDB (local, port 27017) | 11 collections: `users`, `subjects`, `student_progress`, `skill_mastery`, `bkt_params`, `interaction_logs`, `student_clusters`, `problem_difficulty`, `kmeans_models`, `engagement_sessions`, `student_qa` |
| **Vector DB** | ChromaDB (local SQLite, 26 MB) | Embedded vector store for RAG, uses `intfloat/multilingual-e5-base` embeddings |
| **LLM — Content/Quiz/Q&A** | Self-hosted fine-tuned model via Ngrok tunnel | `https://cupbearer-pointing-serotonin.ngrok-free.dev/ask` |
| **LLM — Groq** | Groq Cloud API (`llama-3.3-70b-versatile`) | Used in `llm.py` (currently not directly called in main flow) |
| **TTS** | Google Gemini TTS (`gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts`) | Converts lesson text to WAV audio for avatar |
| **Personalization** | PC-BKT + K-Means + LSTM (optional) | Hybrid Bayesian Knowledge Tracing pipeline |
| **Auth** | JWT + bcrypt (passlib) | Custom signup/login, no OAuth |
| **Static Assets** | 217 PNG images (7 MB), 149 Sinhala text docs (1.3 MB) | Served via FastAPI `StaticFiles` |

### Key Architectural Observations

1. **The fine-tuned Sinhala model** is the critical dependency — hosted externally via Ngrok. This model powers quiz generation, content generation, explanations, and Q&A. You need to decide whether to keep it external or move it to Azure.
2. **ChromaDB** is embedded (file-based SQLite) — it ships with the backend and doesn't need a separate service.
3. **LSTM is optional** — TensorFlow is not installed; the system gracefully falls back to PC-BKT alone.
4. **Frontend is a standard Next.js app** — only needs the backend API URL changed from `localhost:8000` to the Azure backend URL.

