## 3. Azure Service Selection

### 3.1 Frontend: Azure Static Web Apps (Free Tier)

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Why this** | Purpose-built for Next.js. Free SSL, free custom domain, global CDN, GitHub Actions CI/CD built-in |
| **Why not App Service** | App Service would cost $13+/month for a simple frontend. Static Web Apps is free |
| **Why not Azure CDN + Storage** | More complex setup, no built-in SSR support |
| **Free tier** | ✅ 100 GB bandwidth/month, 2 custom domains, free SSL |
| **Estimated cost** | **$0/month** |
| **Code change needed** | Change `API` URL in [api.js](file:///c:/Users/some1/Downloads/FYP_main_project/Sinhala-Teaching-AI-AVATAR/frontend/services/api.js) from `http://127.0.0.1:8000` to your Azure backend URL. Use environment variable instead. |

### 3.2 Backend: Azure App Service (B1 Linux)

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Why this** | Easiest way to deploy a Python FastAPI app. Supports persistent file storage (for ChromaDB), startup commands, environment variables, managed SSL |
| **Why not Container Apps** | Overkill for a single container. Container Apps has cold-start issues on free tier |
| **Why not Azure Functions** | FastAPI is a long-running web server, not suitable for serverless function model |
| **Why not Free (F1) tier** | F1 has 60 min/day CPU limit, no custom domain, no SSL — not production-ready |
| **Plan** | B1 Linux: 1 core, 1.75 GB RAM, 10 GB storage |
| **Estimated cost** | **~$13/month** |
| **Scaling** | Scale up to B2/S1 if needed. Enable autoscale on Standard tier |

> [!NOTE]
> ChromaDB (~26 MB) and static images (~7 MB) and documents (~1.3 MB) will be stored on App Service's persistent storage. Total < 35 MB, well within B1's 10 GB limit.

### 3.3 Database: Azure Cosmos DB for MongoDB (Free Tier)

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Why this** | Your app already uses PyMongo with MongoDB. Cosmos DB for MongoDB is wire-compatible — zero code changes needed |
| **Why not MongoDB Atlas** | Cosmos DB free tier gives 1000 RU/s + 25 GB storage. Atlas free tier gives 512 MB. Cosmos DB wins on capacity and is Azure-native |
| **Why not Azure SQL/PostgreSQL** | Your app is built for MongoDB. Switching would require massive code rewrites |
| **Free tier** | ✅ 1000 RU/s + 25 GB storage, first account per subscription |
| **Estimated cost** | **$0/month** (free tier) |
| **Code change needed** | Change `MONGODB_URI` environment variable in `.env` to Cosmos DB connection string |

### 3.4 Secrets: Azure Key Vault (Free Tier)

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Why this** | Securely store API keys (`GROQ_API_KEY`, `SECRET_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `MONGODB_URI`) instead of `.env` files |
| **Free tier** | ✅ Standard tier: 10,000 transactions/month free |
| **Estimated cost** | **$0/month** |

### 3.5 Monitoring: Application Insights

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Why this** | Built-in with App Service. Tracks request rates, failures, response times, exceptions |
| **Free tier** | ✅ 5 GB/month data ingestion free |
| **Estimated cost** | **$0/month** |

### 3.6 Services NOT Recommended

| Service | Why NOT |
|---------|---------|
| **Azure AI Foundry** | See section 4 below |
| **Azure OpenAI** | You already use Groq (free tier) and a self-hosted fine-tuned model. Azure OpenAI would add ~$5-50/month with no benefit |
| **Azure AI Search** | You already have ChromaDB with multilingual-e5-base embeddings. Azure AI Search starts at $75/month |
| **Azure Front Door** | Overkill for your traffic level. Static Web Apps has built-in CDN |
| **Azure Container Registry** | Not needed unless you containerize. App Service deploys directly from Git |
| **Microsoft Entra ID** | Your app uses custom JWT auth. Adding Entra ID would require frontend and backend rewrites |
| **Azure DNS** | Only needed if you buy a custom domain. Can use free subdomain from Static Web Apps/App Service |

