## 4. Microsoft AI Foundry Integration

### Verdict: **Do NOT use AI Foundry now — revisit when scaling**

| Factor | Analysis |
|--------|----------|
| **Your fine-tuned model** | Stays on your own GPU for now. When ready to scale, use AI Foundry Managed Online Endpoints with NC6s_v3 ($0.90/hr) or NC4as_T4_v3 ($0.53/hr) |
| **Azure OpenAI models** | Don't support Sinhala language at the quality of your fine-tuned model |
| **AI Foundry model catalog** | No Sinhala-specialized models available |
| **Prompt flow** | Your LangGraph pipeline is already built. Migrating to Prompt Flow would require full rewrite |
| **Safety features** | AI Foundry content safety is English-centric. Limited Sinhala support |
| **Cost** | AI Foundry adds Azure OpenAI costs ($5-50/month per model) with minimal benefit |

> [!TIP]
> **Future GPU Migration Path (when you have more users + funding):**
> 1. **Option A — AI Foundry Managed Endpoints:** Deploy your fine-tuned model as a managed endpoint. Use `NC4as_T4_v3` (cheapest GPU) at ~$380/month.
> 2. **Option B — Azure Container Apps with GPU:** Deploy as a container with GPU allocation. More flexible, similar cost.
> 3. **Option C — Azure VM (NC-series):** Rent a GPU VM, run your model server directly. ~$500-700/month but full control.
> 
> **When to migrate:** When your Ngrok tunnel becomes unreliable for production users, or when you need guaranteed uptime/SLA.

**Current Recommendation:** Keep your existing external services (own GPU + Ngrok, Groq API, Google Gemini TTS). They are free or near-free and already working.

