### Step 3: Create Azure Cosmos DB for MongoDB

**Objective:** Replace local MongoDB with cloud-hosted Cosmos DB.

```powershell
# Create Cosmos DB account with MongoDB API and free tier
az cosmosdb create `
  --name cosmos-sinhala-avatar `
  --resource-group rg-sinhala-avatar-prod `
  --kind MongoDB `
  --server-version 4.2 `
  --locations regionName=southeastasia failoverPriority=0 `
  --enable-free-tier true `
  --default-consistency-level Session

# Create the database
az cosmosdb mongodb database create `
  --account-name cosmos-sinhala-avatar `
  --resource-group rg-sinhala-avatar-prod `
  --name ai_avatar `
  --throughput 400
```

**Get Connection String:**
```powershell
az cosmosdb keys list `
  --name cosmos-sinhala-avatar `
  --resource-group rg-sinhala-avatar-prod `
  --type connection-strings `
  --query "connectionStrings[0].connectionString" -o tsv
```

**Verification:** Connect to Cosmos DB from your local machine using the connection string in your `.env` file to test compatibility:
```
MONGODB_URI=<cosmos-db-connection-string>
```

> [!WARNING]
> **Cosmos DB MongoDB compatibility notes:**
> - Your `$group` aggregation pipelines in `clustering_service.py` work fine
> - Unique indexes in `ensure_indexes()` are supported
> - `sort()` operations are supported
> - Test locally first before deploying!

